    <string name="getting_started_with_ranchid">Getting Started with RanchID</string>
    <string name="sign_in_log_in">Sign In / Log In</string>
    <string name="getting_started_text">To log into <b>Ranch.ID</b>, please type the following URL
        in your device web browser: <b>https://naitsng.com</b>. This will lead you to the following page
        shown above</string>
    <string name="getting_started_text_two">\nPlease enter the username and password that were sent to
        you by the administrator and click on the Login button. If you are unable to login, please
        contact <b>09022322237</b> or send email to <b>helpdesk@naits.ng</b></string>
    <string name="dashboard_text">After logging in successfully, all enumerators will be directed to their;\n
        a) Dashboard shows an overview of the data collated at the farm for example: \n1. The number
        of tagged livestock on a farm \n2. The number Livestock owners on a farm </string>
    <string name="enumerator_menu">Enumerator Menu</string>
    <string name="enumerator_text">After logging in successfully, all enumerators will be able to
        click on a menu button at the bottom right corner of the screen and it shows the users the
        available menus on the app</string>
    <string name="register_menu">Register Menu</string>
    <string name="register_text">From the enumerators menu, click on register and it takes you to
        the Register page. The Menu’s on the Register page include : \n1. Add Livestock Owner
        \n2. Add Livestock Keeper \n3. Locations \n4. Tag Livestock \n5. Packing List</string>
    <string name="location_text_one">All livestock tagging exercises take place at pre-designated
        <b>Registration Locations</b>. These registration locations must be created on the
        <b>Ranch.ID</b> system before they can be utilized during enumeration. To create a registration location, click on
        the menu <b>Register => Location</b>. The screens above should appear: </string>
    <string name="location_text_two">\nPlease note that the Application will request you to turn
        on <b>Device Location</b> function on your mobile phone.</string>
    <string name="location_text_three">\nThis is normal, so that the device can
        generate appropriate information on geolocation, as required.</string>
    <string name="location_text_four">\nAlso note that under
        <b>Location Type</b>, you will be required to select: Farm, Ranch, Abattoir, Market or Others After
        filling all the fields in the form, click the <b>Save</b> button.</string>
    <string name="owner_text_one">To create a livestock owner, click on <b>Register => Add</b> Livestock
        Owner on the menu., and this will take you through the various fields to enter information for.
        The various fields are captured above; </string>
    <string name="owner_text_two">\nBe sure to collect the following information:
        NIN, phone number, alternate means of identification both for the owned and for his/her
        next-of-kin. In addition, be sure to select the farm (or location such as ranch, market etc)
        where this livestock owner is located.\n\n<b>Livestock Owner: Passport Photograph</b></string>
    <string name="owner_text_three"><b>Ranch.ID</b> requires you to take a photo of the livestock
        owner as part of the registration process. In order to take the passport photograph, please
        ensure that the livestock owner is standing in front</string>
    <string name="keeper_text_one">In the <b>Ranch.ID</b> platform, every livestock is placed in the
        custody of a Livestock Keeper. To create a livestock keeper, click on <b>Register => Add Livestock Keeper</b>
        on the menu, and this will take you through the various fields to enter information for. The various
        fields are captured below </string>
    <string name="keeper_text_two">\nBe sure to collect the following information: National Identification Number (NIN),
        phone number, alternate means of identification both for the keeper and for his/her next-of-kin.
        In addition, be sure to select the farm (or location such as ranch, market etc) where this
        livestock keeper is located.\n\n<b>Livestock Keeper: Passport Photograph</b></string>
    <string name="keeper_text_three"><b>Ranch.ID</b> requires you to take a photo of the livestock keeper
        as part of the registration process. In order to take the passport photograph, please ensure that
        the livestock keeper is standing in front of a smooth background in a brightly lit area. When
        you are ready, click the \'+\' sign in the camera portion found at the bottom of the page. When
        the camera switches on, click on the <b>Capture Portrait</b> button to take a photo. Finally, click
        the <b>SUBMIT</b> button to create a livestock keeper record.</string>
    <string name="tag_livestock_text">In the Ranch.ID system, livestock are registered by attaching ICAR- compliant,
        Biometric Ear tags onto the livestock’s ears using an applicator, and then taking electronic records afterwards.
        Before tagging any livestock, please ensure that the following information already exists in the system:
        \n\ni) The registration location (farm, ranch, abattoir etc. \n(ii) The livestock owner information
        (individual or group ownership). \niii) The livestock keeper information. \n\nCAUTION: Before tagging very
        large sized livestock, please be sure that you restrain them using crushes! \n\nFor safety purposes,
        first restrain cattle using crushes before tagging Every enumerator shall be assigned a given number of
        plastic livestock tags and also a corresponding number of cattle certificates or passports. For cattle only,
        each Set of Ear Tags shall be assigned to 1 Passport.</string>
    <string name="operations_with_tagged_livestock">Operations with Tagged Livestock</string>
    <string name="scan_for_exit_text_one">Once a livestock has been tagged and recorded in the Ranch.ID system,
        several operations can be carried out. \n\n<b>a) Scan for Abattoir Exit</b></string>
    <string name="scan_for_exit_text_two">Animals meant to be slaughtered at abattoirs must first be
        exited from the Ranch.ID database. Marking a tagged livestock as \'exited\' means that the livestock is dead.
        The operation of exiting a livestock at an abattoir or other locations will help in ensuring
        the integrity of the data in the Ranch.ID database.</string>
    <string name="scan_for_exit_text_three">\nTo scan for abattoir exit, click on <b>Tags => Scan for Exit (Abattoir)</b>
        Next, scan the QR code on the given tag. If the scan is successful, the livestock information will be
        displayed on a modal pop-up box. Thereafter, enter the livestock health status, and then select the exit location.
        Finally, press the SUBMIT button to exit the livestock.</string>
    <string name="scan_for_exit_text_four"><b>To scan for abattoir exit</b>, click on <b>Tags => Scan for Exit (Abattoir)</b> </string>
    <string name="scan_for_exit_text_five">Next, scan the QR code on the given tag. If the scan is successful,
        the livestock information will be displayed on a modal pop-up box. \n\nThereafter, enter the livestock health status,
        and then select the exit location. \n\nFinally, press the SUBMIT button to exit the livestock.</string>
    <string name="packing_list_text_one">Once a livestock has been tagged and recorded in the Ranch.ID system,
        several operations can be carried out. \n\n<b>a) Scan for Packing List</b></string>
    <string name="packing_list_text_two">Animals meant to be transported from one location to another
        must be documented in the RanchID Database. Every important information abut the livestock to
        be transported  is documented.This operation helps ensure integrity of the Ranch ID Database.\n\n</string>
    <string name="packing_list_text_three">To scan for Packing List, click on <b>Register => Packing list</b>.
        Next scan the QR Code on the given tag. If the scan is successful,the livestock information is uploaded
        automatically and the farmer can go on to scan a different livestock. This process is repeated until all
        animals are scanned and counted. Press the SUBMIT button to proceed. </string>
